\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Anything convenient, including a set-level definition of (augmented) virtual double categories and of free ones. These exist \em{only} to construct shape categories and to state the self-hosting theorem; they are not the library's notion of VDC, which is the discrete case of the root (→ \ref{dec-rt-0011}). Kernel files are marked \code{-- KERNEL} and live under \code{Kernel/}.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Weber's construction of shape categories needs the algebras whose free objects the shapes are (→ \ref{dec-kr-0003}). Refusing to write set-level VDCs in the kernel would force an ad hoc tree combinatorics as the \em{definition} of \code{Θ_fc} and make the nerve theorem a correctness gamble instead of an instance of a general theorem.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen.}
}
